  "steps": [
    "Bring a large pot of well-salted water to the boil and cook the pasta until al dente. Reserve a cup of pasta water before draining.",
    "Meanwhile, warm the olive oil in a deep pan over medium heat. Soften the onion for 6–7 minutes until translucent, then add the garlic and cook for one more minute.",
    "Stir in the tomato purée and cook for a minute to deepen the colour, then pour in the chopped tomatoes. Simmer gently for 12 minutes.",
    "Blend the soaked cashews with the oat milk until completely smooth. Stir this cream through the sauce along with the oregano and chilli flakes.",
    "Tip the drained pasta into the sauce, loosening with a splash of pasta water until it coats every piece. Season to taste.",
    "Fold through the torn basil off the heat and serve with extra pepper."
  ],
  "notes": "Soak the cashews in just-boiled water for 15 minutes if you forgot to do it overnight — they'll still blend silky. The sauce freezes beautifully for up to 3 months."
}
